course: dictionary
lesson: 12205
title: Food from around the world
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name food that people eat in other countries. You may not know them, but the sentences around them often give clues. «Mei had a warm bowl of congee for breakfast.» A bowl is for eating something runny or soft, and breakfast is a meal in the morning, so congee is probably a food you eat in the morning.
explain: «When Ben had a cold, his nan made him plain congee.» Nan made it because Ben was poorly, and the word plain tells you it had no extra toppings. Clues like these help you work out what a word means without a dictionary.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Try «Mei had a warm bowl of a thick, soft rice porridge for breakfast.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is probably right.
fact: Congee is a thick, soft rice porridge.
fact: It is made by cooking rice in lots of water for a long time.
fact: Congee is eaten across China and East and South-East Asia.
fact: People often eat congee for breakfast, or when someone is ill, because it is soft and gentle.
fact: In Chinese, congee is called «zhou» or «jook».
exercise: «Mei had a warm bowl of congee for breakfast.» What is congee? | *A thick, soft rice porridge | A crispy fried bread | A sweet cake from a bakery | A cold salad with vegetables
exercise: In Chinese, congee is also called «zhou» or «jook». Which of these is another name for congee? | noodle | dumpling | bread | *jook
exercise: «When Ben had a cold, his nan made him plain congee.» Why did his nan make him congee? | Because it is hard and crunchy | Because Ben asked for a sweet cake | *Because it is soft and gentle when you feel poorly | Because congee is always eaten at midnight
test: Congee is made by cooking lots of rice in a lot of water for a long time. What is the main ingredient? | Pasta | *Rice | Oats | Potatoes
test: Where is congee eaten? | Only in Italy | Only in Australia | Only in Scotland | *Across China and East and South-East Asia
exam: «Congee is often eaten for breakfast, or when someone is poorly.» Which words in this sentence show when congee is eaten? | *for breakfast or when someone is poorly | cooked in lots of water | thick and soft | eaten across China
